      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "French explorers navigated the Black River after the 1803 Louisiana Purchase, establishing a lasting presence that led to Peach Orchard.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_Orchard%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When the Louis, Iron Mountain and Southern Railroad reached Peach Orchard in the 1870s, a post office opened in 1873 and a depot followed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
